{
  "id": "Compound::DB00162 - Gene::50700",
  "verbalization": "Vitamin A is implicated in the interaction with Rdh8 through a shared pathway involving Nadp-retinol dehydrogenase activity. The evidence suggests that Vitamin A binds to Dhrs3 or Rdh11, both of which participate in Nadp-retinol dehydrogenase activity, which in turn is participated by Rdh8. This indicates a potential functional link between Vitamin A and Rdh8 through a common intermediate, Nadp-retinol dehydrogenase activity. The presence of multiple pathways converging on Rdh8 suggests that Vitamin A may influence Rdh8 through a mechanism involving retinol metabolism, possibly by modulating the activity of the Nadp-retinol dehydrogenase enzyme. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible role for Vitamin A in regulating Rdh8 function, though the exact nature of this regulation remains to be elucidated.",
